          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "An unusually tall, heavy-bodied deer with wide, palmed antlers and a long muzzle."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Attacks",
          "lines": [
            "Hooves · melee · +6 to hit · reach 5 ft. · 1d8 + 4 bludgeoning"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Trait mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Forest Walker · The moose has advantage on DEX (Stealth) checks in forest terrain."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Action mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Hooves · If it moves at least 10 ft. straight toward a Large or smaller creature immediately before hitting it, the hit deals an extra 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage and knocks the target prone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Reaction mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Fury · Taking at least 5 damage gives the moose advantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "Black Flag fixed values are Perception 13 and Stealth 10. Ability modifiers are STR +4, DEX +0, CON +2, INT −4, WIS +1 and CHA −3. No languages or special senses.",
            "The Northlanders also call this animal Elg. The book describes it as nearly 7 ft. at the shoulder.",
            "Source: Kobold Press, Northlands Worldbook (2026, Tales of the Valiant), p. 264."
          ]
        }
      ],
